  "caveats": [
    "y_λ is NOT sign-definite at n=9 (10 of 30 weights negative), so a block's Δ²_λ<0 may come from submodular geometry OR from supermodular geometry carried by a negative weight. Only the former is a Fréchet violation; the two are reported separately. Consequently the Lean lemma reweight_cannot_open_door (hypothesis w_λ ≥ 0) does not apply to this spectrum.",
    "Measurement only. No Δ_λ closure, no μ₃ value fitted, nothing wired to production."
  ]
